2026-05-27 11:25:13,956 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-05-27 11:25:13,957 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: Based on our company context, I propose leveraging our expertise in large language models (LLMs) and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities to provide intelligent assistance to agents. We can deploy a model like Mistral 7B Instruct, which is our preferred sovereign model, to generate high-quality answers. To improve the relevance of these answers, we can fine-tune this model using our LoRA or QLoRA methods on a domain-specific corpus, which has shown to provide an average accuracy gain of 12%. 

To further enhance the solution, we can integrate RAG capabilities, utilizing retrieval strategies such as dense vector semantic search or BM25 sparse search, and chunking strategies like recursive text splitter or semantic chunking. This will enable the system to effectively search for information within internal procedures and regulations, provide assistance with drafting letters or answers, and accompany agents in the instruction of files.

To ensure the quality and relevance of the answers, we can employ our explainability and trust methods, including source citation, chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, and LIME. Additionally, we will implement confidence scoring, with a low-confidence threshold of 0.65, and display uncertainty warnings when necessary, escalating to human supervisors as required.

Our innovation pipeline, currently exploring topics like knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning and multi-agent collaboration frameworks, can also contribute to the long-term enhancement of this solution, potentially integrating new research findings and advancements in AI over the project duration. By leveraging these components and strategies, we aim to provide a comprehensive and effective intelligent assistance tool that meets the client's requirements while ensuring the quality and relevance of the answers provided.
